Subject: [PATCH] configure: disable POSIX feature macros for Darwin cross-builds

When cross-compiling for Darwin, ac_sys_release is empty. The
existing Darwin version patterns therefore do not match, causing
configure to define _POSIX_C_SOURCE and _XOPEN_SOURCE.

On Darwin these macros hide non-POSIX APIs, including sendfile(),
from system headers.

Handle the empty release explicitly, preserving the existing
behavior for native builds.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -835,6 +835,9 @@
     define_xopen_source=no;;
   Darwin/@<:@[12]@:>@@<:@0-9@:>@.*)
     define_xopen_source=no;;
+  # Cross-compilation does not provide ac_sys_release.
+  Darwin/)
+    define_xopen_source=no;;
   # On iOS, defining _POSIX_C_SOURCE also disables platform specific features.
   iOS/*)
     define_xopen_source=no;;
diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -4403,6 +4403,9 @@
     define_xopen_source=no;;
   Darwin/[12][0-9].*)
     define_xopen_source=no;;
+  # Cross-compilation does not provide ac_sys_release.
+  Darwin/)
+    define_xopen_source=no;;
   # On iOS, defining _POSIX_C_SOURCE also disables platform specific features.
   iOS/*)
     define_xopen_source=no;;
